.SS " bool pip\&._internal\&.resolution\&.legacy\&.resolver\&.Resolver\&._is_upgrade_allowed ( self, \fBInstallRequirement\fP req)\fC [protected]\fP"

.SS " None pip\&._internal\&.resolution\&.legacy\&.resolver\&.Resolver\&._populate_link ( self, \fBInstallRequirement\fP req)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Ensure that if a link can be found for this, that it is found\&.

Note that req\&.link may still be None - if the requirement is already
installed and not needed to be upgraded based on the return value of
_is_upgrade_allowed()\&.

If preparer\&.require_hashes is True, don't use the wheel cache, because
cached wheels, always built locally, have different hashes than the
files downloaded from the index server and thus throw false hash
mismatches\&. Furthermore, cached wheels at present have undeterministic
contents due to file modification times\&.

.fi
